---
import { PdfComponent } from "../components/pdf.component";
import Layout from "../layout/Layout.astro";
const title = 'Convert HEIC to PDF Online — One Photo per Page';
const description = 'Turn HEIC photos into one PDF with a page per selected file. Convert locally, download the document and check page order, readability and file size.';
const ogImage = "/og-image/heic-to-pdf.png";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} ogImage={ogImage} ogTitle={title}>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4">
    <h1 class="text-center font-bold text-4xl mt-12 mb-5">Convert HEIC to PDF</h1>
    <p class="text-center text-zinc-700 mb-8">Create a PDF when a recipient asks for a document. Select one or more HEIC photos; the tool places each photo on its own page in one PDF.</p>
    <PdfComponent client:visible />
    <section class="mt-12 mb-10 prose max-w-none" aria-labelledby="conversion-steps">
      <h2 id="conversion-steps">How to convert HEIC to PDF</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Choose <strong>Choose files</strong> and select the HEIC photos on your device.</li>
        <li>Wait for conversion to finish. It starts automatically after selection.</li>
        <li>When the Download link appears, save output.pdf and open it in a PDF viewer.</li>
        <li>Check the downloaded result before sharing it. Choose <strong>Convert More</strong> to start another batch.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Selected photo bytes are processed locally in your browser rather than uploaded to a conversion server. The website still loads its scripts and other web resources. No account or conversion fee is required.</p>
      <p>For alternatives and troubleshooting, read the <a href="/blog/heic-to-pdf/">HEIC to PDF guide</a> and <a href="/how-it-works/">how conversion works</a>.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="prose max-w-none mb-10" aria-labelledby="conversion-limits">
      <h2 id="conversion-limits">What to check before using the result</h2>
      <p>This is an image-only PDF, made with a fixed JPEG quality setting. It does not perform OCR or create selectable text. Pages follow image proportions rather than a fixed A4 or Letter size. There are no margin, crop, paper-size or target-file-size controls.</p>
      <p>Large photos or batches can need substantial memory. If conversion fails, try a single complete HEIC file, then a smaller batch. Support can vary with the HEIC variant, browser and available device memory.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="prose max-w-none mb-16" aria-labelledby="format-choice">
      <h2 id="format-choice">When to choose PDF</h2>
      <p>Check every page in a PDF viewer before uploading it. The tool follows the file list supplied by the browser; there is no page-reordering control. Confirm the recipient's page and size requirements. Keep your HEIC originals.</p>
      <p>Compare <a href="/blog/heic-jpg-png-pdf-which-format/">JPG, PNG, WebP and PDF</a>, or use the <a href="/blog/heic-photo-upload-not-supported/">photo upload checklist</a> if a form still rejects your file.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
